xt": "Tneed**.\nThursday,\nftatonfeY*"}, {"id": "p4b23", "x": 11.603, "y": 13.314, "w": 1.918, "h": 0.463, "text": "Vftp. to."}, {"id": "p4b24", "x": 4.706, "y": 13.874, "w": 1.281, "h": 0.543, "text": "'\u2022Ste"}, {"id": "p4b25", "x": 14.246, "y": 13.032, "w": 2.869, "h": 1.094, "text": "Monday.\nWednesday,\nFndayy"}, {"id": "p4b26", "x": 17.735, "y": 13.314, "w": 1.698, "h": 0.463, "text": "V* 90 a."}, {"id": "p4b27", "x": 8.271, "y": 14.295, "w": 12.015, "h": 1.586, "text": "Conches leaving Medora connect with east\nbound passenger rr&ln.\nCoaches arriving at Medora connect with west\nbotrod passenger train."}, {"id": "p4b28", "x": 8.242, "y": 16.47, "w": 10.577, "h": 2.357, "text": "Northern Pacific Time Table.\nWIST BOUXD.\nPacific Express, No. 1....\nExpress freight, 2d Class\nFreight, 3dClase"}, {"id": "p4b29", "x": 5.344, "y": 19.765, "w": 1.368, "h": 0.543, "text": "mm"}, {"id": "p4b30", "x": 17.399, "y": 17.661, "w": 2.179, "h": 0.463, "text": "...6:47p."}, {"id": "p4b31", "x": 8.305, "y": 19.487, "w": 12.107, "h": 1.161, "text": "AtianttcBxprese,No., 3 8:48 a. m.\nExpressFreight,8dClass ...7:00p, m.\nFreight, SrdClBes.... .1:45p m*"}, {"id": "p4b32", "x": 14.246, "y": 20.75, "w": 5.593, "h": 0.463, "text": "J. N. Maxwell, Agent."}, {"id": "p4b33", "x": 8.386, "y": 21.941, "w": 12.084, "h": 2.365, "text": "Dnck and geese are plentiful up and\ndown the river.\nCharlie Jolly is nearly recovered from\nhis recent injury."}, {"id": "p4b34", "x": 8.404, "y": 24.394, "w": 12.154, "h": 2.925, "text": "F. W. McKinney, of Bismarck, stopped\nover a train Tuesday.\nMcKenzier ft O'Brien will soon mpve\ntheir blacksmith shop to this side of the\ntrack, .r \u2022\u2022,"}, {"id": "p4b35", "x": 8.421, "y": 27.411, "w": 12.142, "h": 1.662, "text": "DanMcKenzie returned Monday even\ning from a three months' trip to Nora\nScotia. v.."}, {"id": "p4b36", "x": 8.375, "y": 29.233, "w": 12.142, "h": 1.662, "text": "The stock-yards are completed but are\nscarcely- large enongh to receive three\ncar-loads of cattle."}, {"id": "p4b37", "x": 8.386, "y": 30.988, "w": 12.102, "h": 1.662, "text": "Dr. Hebar Bobart, of Dickinson, came\nup last night to see Mrs. Draper who has\nbeen ill for some time."}, {"id": "p4b38", "x": 8.421, "y": 32.882, "w": 12.038, "h": 1.662, "text": "Again were the remaining shoots of\nthe delinquent contestants put off on\naccount of the rain Saturday."}, {"id": "p4b39", "x": 8.462, "y": 34.704, "w": 12.055, "h": 2.226, "text": "Tom Matthews stopped off a- train\nMonday. He has been appointed inspec\ntor by the Montana board of stock com\nmissioners."}, {"id": "p4b40", "x": 8.508, "y": 37.09, "w": 12.009, "h": 2.222, "text": "Those who have been shootiug in the\nrink for prizes must have their scores\ncompleted by May 1, as the prizes are\ngiven on that day."}, {"id": "p4b41", "x": 8.531, "y": 39.404, "w": 11.957, "h": 2.222, "text": "Jack Bullion's brother, Robert, from\nMaryland Junction, Mmn., has been here\nseveral days. He intends putting in\nsome horses with Jack."}, {"id": "p4b42", "x": 8.549, "y": 41.79, "w": 12.009, "h": 2.222, "text": "Large eorralls have been built both\nhere and on Sally creek, in addition to\nthe othere the Co. has, to accommodate\nthe cattle here this summer."}, {"id": "p4b43", "x": 8.618, "y": 44.172, "w": 11.997, "h": 2.226, "text": "It almost breaks my heart to be the\nbearer of this sad newB. Would that I\ncould suffer for you.\" Ask the night\nteleg. to diagram this \"goak.\""}, {"id": "p4b44", "x": 8.444, "y": 46.558, "w": 12.258, "h": 2.786, "text": "It is entirely feasible to bore an arte\nsian we'd here and the water will be\nentirely free from alkali. We will have\nsomething more to say about this matter\n\u2022\u2022soon. ..."}, {"id": "p4b45", "x": 8.647, "y": 49.432, "w": 12.044, "h": 2.786, "text": "Word has been received from the Wil\nlard Broa* that they will be here Satur\nday or Sunday, with several car-loads of\nhorses. Several sales have been missed\nby their delay in coming."}, {"id": "p4b46", "x": 8.375, "y": 52.378, "w": 12.443, "h": 4.027, "text": "W. H. McKanlasa, the colored skater\nand musician will give an exhibition at\nthe rink to-morrow evening, which prom\nises to be a very interesting entertain\nment. His performance is highly spoken\n.of by the papers along the line.\n\"1: J."}, {"id": "p4b47", "x": 9.957, "y": 55.605, "w": 0.609, "h": 0.77, "text": "c."}, {"id": "p4b48", "x": 6.364, "y": 63.529, "w": 1.588, "h": 0.543, "text": "St\u00ae"}, {"id": "p4b49", "x": 6.01, "y": 64.232, "w": 2.029, "h": 0.539, "text": "^lll1"}, {"id": "p4b50", "x": 6.097, "y": 65.355, "w": 1.774, "h": 1.098, "text": "\u2022\"\u2022ifS\n$\u00a3$\u00bb?\u2022"}, {"id": "p4b51", "x": 5.987, "y": 66.756, "w": 1.936, "h": 1.401, "text": "'mk\nMM"}, {"id": "p4b52", "x": 10.769, "y": 55.816, "w": 9.969, "h": 0.539, "text": "Fisher has already set a good ex\u00ad"}, {"id": "p4b53", "x": 8.636, "y": 56.375, "w": 12.102, "h": 2.786, "text": "ample which we hope to see followed ex\ntensively. Arbor day, the 25th. Several\nhave already made np their minds to set\nout treeB, which will do much toward\nimproving the looks of our town."}, {"id": "p4b54", "x": 8.711, "y": 59.321, "w": 12.107, "h": 3.838, "text": "Miss Lou Eleson, of Glendive, will be\nhere Tuesday and Wednesday the 28th.\nand HMJl, with a complete assortment of\nladies'millinery and fancy goods. Any\nthing desired in this line will be on sale\nand it will be an excellent opportunity\nto boy."}, {"id": "p4b55", "x": 8.711, "y": 63.318, "w": 12.136, "h": 3.909, "text": "A meeting will be held next Monday\nevening at the rink to organize a bucket\nbrigade. The. movement is a commenda\nble one and it behooves all onr citizens\nto turn out to the meeting. We-are lia\nbleat any time to have afire and effect\nual work can be done with buckets."}, {"id": "p4b56", "x": 8.097, "y": 67.459, "w": 12.843, "h": 7.974, "text": "To-night at. the rink there will be\ntournament, the person securing the great\ncat number of rings to be given a prize\nSaturday evening May 2, there will be a\nmasquerade, many of the participants in\nthe lastone desiring a repetition. Admis\nsion to both entertainments will be only\n:\u201ethe usnal rates'.\n*5', The post-office hae been again moved\nto it* old location in the Co's store. The\nchange will not be popular, as lock and\ncall boxes possess manv advantages over\nthe general delivery system: It is also\nrather severe on Mr. Fishery \"wich wuz"}, {"id": "p4b57", "x": 6.242, "y": 69.631, "w": 1.814, "h": 0.311, "text": "\u2022fc"}, {"id": "p4b58", "x": 6.126, "y": 69.984, "w": 1.918, "h": 0.846, "text": "vpR'"}, {"id": "p4b59", "x": 8.085, "y": 75.454, "w": 12.739, "h": 2.853, "text": "P. MV as he had gone to ctmbideable ex\npense in .fitting up the office in the rink.\nThe roand-vp out of the river and\n., north of the Jtraekvand. to inclnde the\nwholr KilldeW 'Mtf country will begin"}, {"id": "p4b60", "x": 8.653, "y": 78.329, "w": 12.136, "h": 3.345, "text": "May t. This round-up is for the purpose\n\u00abt driving all. the.cattle possible.to the\nriver seas to be eanght in our general\nround-up. Tfee date for a corresponding\nround-op south of the track has not been\ndecided. .:"}, {"id": "p4b61", "x": 8.131, "y": 81.767, "w": 12.693, "h": 2.782, "text": "Wenotice in the St. Panl dispatcher\nthat day before yesterday a number of\nprominent cowmen were contracting\nwith theft P. for the delivery of40,000cat\n.. tie to Medora from Washington territory."}, {"id": "p4b62", "x": 8.578, "y": 84.569, "w": 12.096, "h": 2.786, "text": "On aeeoont ot the large number of cattle\nand the fact that Wveral of the cowmen\nmentioned have all their herds in Mon\niiasa, we ate Inclined to discredit the\nWport"}, {"id": "p4b63", "x": 8.647, "y": 87.515, "w": 12.102, "h": 4.961, "text": "The rainy, drfcnty, gnowy weather of\nSaturday, Sunday,, Monday and Tuesday,\n-was a perfect godsend to western Dakota.\nTh* rain came scarcely tester than need\nt\u00bb to hate every, drop soak into the\nground and this, followed by the damp\nsnow of \"Ttteeday and melted by yester\nday's genial weather will OQ the ground\nfall as it can hold of water. One ean"}, {"id": "p4b64", "x": 11.024, "y": 93.057, "w": 0.614, "h": 0.387, "text": "\u2022a"}, {"id": "p4b65", "x": 11.099, "y": 93.267, "w": 3.593, "h": 0.77, "text": "i^Wt."}, {"id": "p4b66", "x": 7.807, "y": 95.931, "w": 0.411, "h": 0.774, "text": "e-"}, {"id": "p4b67", "x": 28.689, "y": 3.425, "w": 4.648, "h": 1.852, "text": "\u00a718^111111"}, {"id": "p4b68", "x": 20.662, "y": 5.95, "w": 12.154, "h": 2.365, "text": "Lee Eisenberg, of Bismarck, was here\nSaturday with a line of dry goods.\nArthur Smith has almost recovered\nfrom his accident of two weeks ago."}, {"id": "p4b69", "x": 20.749, "y": 8.475, "w": 12.067, "h": 1.591, "text": "Geo. Porter returned from Chicago last\nFriday night. His wife will return in\nabout ten days."}, {"id": "p4b70", "x": 20.731, "y": 10.23, "w": 12.2, "h": 2.15, "text": "Theodore Roosevelt came in last Fri\nday night and started almost immedia\ntely for his Elkhorn ranch down the\nriver."}, {"id": "p4b71", "x": 20.818, "y": 12.612, "w": 12.159, "h": 4.54, "text": "Wal. Osterhout went to Miles, Sunday\nvening to arrange for some horses for\niloward Faton, who went up Monday\nlight.\n\"Sadie\" Honk, who'will be remembered\nas a Cow BOT comp. last summer passed\nthrough Saturday uighton his way to\nalendive.-"}, {"id": "p4b72", "x": 20.853, "y": 17.312, "w": 12.142, "h": 2.714, "text": "J. D. Garver returned from Bismarck\nlast Friday, with his family. His wife's\nhealth is improved though she is far from\nwell. His sister-in-law also accompanied\nhim."}, {"id": "p4b73", "x": 19.723, "y": 17.804, "w": 0.661, "h": 0.307, "text": "TO,"}, {"id": "p4b74", "x": 17.486, "y": 18.015, "w": 2.828, "h": 0.812, "text": "...5:00a. m.\n..11:40 a."}, {"id": "p4b75", "x": 12.751, "y": 18.924, "w": 3.217, "h": 0.463, "text": "KAST BOUND."}, {"id": "p4b76", "x": 20.934, "y": 20.258, "w": 12.119, "h": 2.714, "text": "If by any chance a subscriber should\nnot get his paper, it would be a favor if\nthe fact were immediately reported to\nthis office. We will rectify any mistake\nof this nature."}, {"id": "p4b77", "x": 20.952, "y": 23.203, "w": 12.183, "h": 2.714, "text": "The body of Mrs. Hawkins, of Spearfish,\nPresident Garfield's niece, was brought\nup on the.coach Saturday night from\nSpearfish and shipped to Mrs. Garfield at\nCleveland, Ohio."}, {"id": "p4b78", "x": 20.963, "y": 26.149, "w": 12.206, "h": 2.714, "text": "B. J. Matthias, formerly superinten\ndent 6f this division of the N. P. is pres\nident of the Charlotte Harbor and North\nern CeatraL R. R. with1 headquarters at\nTampa^Florida."}, {"id": "p4b79", "x": 30.097, "y": 28.392, "w": 0.081, "h": 0.311, "text": "1"}, {"id": "p4b80", "x": 20.894, "y": 29.023, "w": 12.241, "h": 6.224, "text": "Mr. Ti'Martin will make a complete\ndigest of his weather reports for the last\nsix months,\nto be published in connection\nwith! his monthly reports. It will moke\na valuable paper for reference.\n'Skinny\" Wallace, who drives on the\nstage line from Buffalo creek to Middle\nGrand river, was in town Saturday.\nWhile here he laid in a good supply of\npoint and spread a thin coat over the\nsuburbs."}, {"id": "p4b81", "x": 20.923, "y": 35.406, "w": 12.275, "h": 3.905, "text": "Rer. H. B. Schaffner preached an elo\nquent sermon in the rink last Snnday\nevening to a small congregetion. The\nweather was very stormy which doubtless\naccounts for the few in attendance. Ser\nvice will be held every Sunday evening\nhereafter, at half-past seven."}, {"id": "p4b82", "x": 20.969, "y": 39.476, "w": 12.281, "h": 4.465, "text": "Lloyd Roberts returned from Glendive\nMonday morning and started for St.\nCloud again Tuesday morning. He\ndelivered several hundred cattle in Glen\ndive in prime condition. He has also\ndelivered mixed herds in Jamestown and\nBismarck.. He will return again about\nMay 10."}, {"id": "p4b83", "x": 21.039, "y": 44.105, "w": 12.2, "h": 5.029, "text": "Our thanks are due A.McCall of the\nBlack Hills for a complete list of house\nand council bills passed at the last ses\nsion of the legislature. Mr. McCall,\noriginated and with the able assistance\nof the other Hills members, had the bill\npassed repealing the herd law and estab\nlishing the fence law the western tier\nof counties."}, {"id": "p4b84", "x": 21.137, "y": 49.293, "w": 12.148, "h": 5.029, "text": "Mr. and Mrs. and Miss Hattie Eaton\nparents and. sister of the Eattfn boys,\ncame in Monday evening and for the\nsummer will, make their headquarter^ at\nthe logging\ncamp. Mr. Eaton reported that\nwhile we were having splendid weather\nhere, they were having the worst wcath-,\ner in the east, that he ever experienced.\nFor a time it almost paralyzed business."}, {"id": "p4b85", "x": 21.085, "y": 54.414, "w": 12.183, "h": 5.588, "text": "Last Friday evening, No. 1 was delayed\nseven or eight hours by the falling of a\nhuge rock upon the track just east of\nSully Springs. A serious accident nearly\nresulted, as the train could not be stopped\nuntil the engine had struck the rock and\nthrew the two front drivers off the track.\nThe rock should have been blasted off\nlong ago as it has been threatening to\nfall for two or-three years."}, {"id": "p4b86", "x": 23.832, "y": 60.655, "w": 6.74, "h": 0.539, "text": "Freighters Attention I"}, {"id": "p4b87", "x": 21.212, "y": 61.568, "w": 11.893, "h": 1.873, "text": "Be sure and take your watch to the\nKing jeweler, Spearfish or Deadwood for\nrepairs."}, {"id": "p4b88", "x": 23.676, "y": 64.37, "w": 6.995, "h": 0.543, "text": "Drags, Paints and Oils."}, {"id": "p4b89", "x": 21.253, "y": 64.934, "w": 11.899, "h": 1.662, "text": "People who may want any of the\nabove articles, will do well to corres\npond with,"}, {"id": "p4b90", "x": 24.846, "y": 66.546, "w": 6.462, "h": 1.17, "text": "FRANK FBISBY,\nBismarck, Dak."}, {"id": "p4b91